    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This seems like a large and intrusive change for what should be a niche use case. (Something LLMs _love_ to do, as they only ever focus on the task at hand and have no holistic concept of code base quality...)\r\n\r\nWouldn't it be easier to simply (optionally) destroy and recreate the highlighter in the query manipulation functions? (As a general rule: don't make everyone pay the price for a niche.)",
