        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@clason That's a fair callout. Instead of destroying and recreating highlighters, what if there's a C-to-lua refresh function that clears the conceal marks and cached state instead? That would be less invasive. My concern is `destroy()` leaves parser callbacks registered, so repeated recreation would accumulate callbacks. Refreshing existing instances avoid that. Do you agree?",
